# Extracted archive contents — regenerated from data/raw on demand
data/processed/extracted/

# Derived spatial database, QGIS project and rendered maps — all rebuilt
# from data/raw by re-running the scripts. output/data_profile.md is kept
# deliberately, so the data review is readable without running anything.
data/processed/*.gpkg
data/processed/*.gpkg-shm
data/processed/*.gpkg-wal
data/processed/*.qgs
data/smoothed/*.gpkg
data/smoothed/*.qgs

# Copernicus DEM — kept in the repository deliberately. It is public
# Copernicus data and scripts/fetch_dem.py can re-fetch it, but the
# hillshade under every map depends on it, and a container that loses it
# renders the overview maps flat without anything failing. 19 MB once is
# cheaper than a map quietly losing its terrain.
output/*.png
# Query pack is a deliverable that goes to the field — keep it tracked
!output/queries/
output/*.html

# QGIS working files
*.qgs~
*.qgz~
*.qgd

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Sacred site locations are never shared — reported by area only.
data/smoothed/*sacred*
output/*sacred*.gpkg

# npm working files for the Word report build
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Report data feeding the Word documents — small, and worth keeping so a
# document can be traced back to the figures it was built from.
!output/report/
!output/walkers/

# GPX going back to the Clan Stewards — a deliverable, kept tracked
!output/gpx/

# The GPX bundle is a zip of output/gpx/, rebuilt by scripts/clan_gpx.py.
# Tracking it would store the same data twice, once per version.
output/*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is kept and what is not.
#
# Kept, because it cannot be made again: the raw archives, every
# register of what was decided, the stored boundaries, the maps the
# reviewer agreed under a round, and the report's own figures. Those are
# the record, and the repository is where the record lives — more
# durable than any working session.
#
# Not kept, because running the pipeline makes it again: the built Word
# documents and the rendered map images. They are large, they change on
# every build, and keeping them put hundreds of megabytes of pictures
# into a public repository to no purpose.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Built documents — rebuilt by scripts/build_reports.py
output/*.docx

# Rendered query and clan maps — rebuilt by the pipeline. output/rounds/
# and output/clans/approved/ are NOT ignored: those are the maps that
# went to a clan, and a map that moves after it was shown is not that
# map any more.
output/queries/
output/clans/*.png

# Sacred sites are reported to the landowners and the reviewer, and to
# nobody else. Nothing naming or locating one belongs in a repository.
output/sacred_sites.md
output/queries/*sacred*
